# Localization (Doable Habits)

This app supports **in-app language switching** (`AppSettings.appLanguageKey` → `AppLocaleModifier`). System locale and SwiftUI `\.locale` alone are not enough for user-visible strings.

## Golden rules

1. **Never resolve UI copy with bare `String(localized:)`** — it ignores the app language and freezes at first render.
2. **Prefer `Text("Catalog key")` / `LocalizedStringKey`** in SwiftUI — respects `\.locale` from `AppLocaleModifier`.
3. **For `String` output** (labels passed as `String`, notifications, widgets): use `LocalizedFormat` + `AppLocale.current`.
4. **Never store localized `String` in ViewModels** — store catalog **keys**; localize in the view layer.
5. **Never bake localized text into snapshots/models** — store keys or enums; format at display time.

## APIs to use

```swift
// Static UI label (preferred)
Text("Daily goal")

// Label + dynamic suffix
Text("Goal") + Text(verbatim: ": \(habit.targetValue)")

// Formatted String when Text is not an option
LocalizedFormat.format("%lld habit", arguments: [count])
LocalizedFormat.string("Skipped today")

// App language source of truth
AppLocale.current
AppLocale.identifier
```

Do **not** add a second localization helper unless `LocalizedFormat` / `AppLocale` is insufficient.

## SwiftUI refresh on language change

- Add `@AppStorage(AppSettings.appLanguageKey)` to views that show pre-formatted `String` values.
- Pass locale into **sheets**: `.environment(\.locale, sheetLocale)`.
- Force List rebuild when needed: `.id(appLanguageRawValue)` on the list/section.
- `sheetLocale`: use `Locale(identifier: appLanguageRawValue)` when not `.system`, else `\.locale`.

## String Catalog (`Localizable.xcstrings`)

- Main app: `doablehabits/Localizable.xcstrings`
- Widgets: `doablehabitsWidgets/Localizable.xcstrings`
- **Empty entries `{}` fall back to English** — fill all 33 locales:  
  `ar, ca, cs, da, de, el, en, es-MX, fi, fr, he, hi, hr, hu, id, it, ja, ko, ms, nb, nl, pl, pt-BR, ro, ru, sk, sv, th, tr, uk, vi, zh-Hans, zh-Hant`
- Use **plural variations** in the catalog for count strings (`one` / `few` / `many` / `other`) — do not hardcode Russian/Polish plurals in Swift `if count == 1`.
- After adding keys, verify with a script or audit — no `<ph id='…'/>` placeholders; keep `%lld` in format keys.

## Anti-patterns

```swift
// BAD — frozen system locale
Text(habit.goalSummaryText)
String(localized: "Goal")
viewModel.message = String(localized: "Nice job")

// BAD — split localized sentence across views without catalog plural rules
Text("To record:") + Text("\(n)") + Text("days")

// GOOD
HabitGoalSummaryLabel(habit: habit)
LocalizedFormat.format("To record: %lld days", arguments: [n])
GentleFeedbackView(messageKey: "Nice job")
```

## Checklist before finishing localization work

- [ ] New keys exist in the correct `.xcstrings` with all 33 locales
- [ ] UI uses `Text`/`LocalizedStringKey` or `LocalizedFormat` + `AppLocale`
- [ ] ViewModels expose keys, not localized strings
- [ ] Sheets/lists update after language change (`@AppStorage`, `.id`, sheet locale)
- [ ] Build succeeds; manually switch ru ↔ en on affected screens
